WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:08.766
You can now access Knox E-FOTA firmware management capabilities on Microsoft Intune, giving you flexible control over OS versions and 

2
00:00:08.766 --> 00:00:13.999
security updates on your fleet of Samsung devices, right from the Microsoft Intune admin center.

3
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:21.000
To use Knox E-FOTA, you must first sign up for a Samsung Knox account on samsungknox.com.

4
00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:27.699
When getting started, select "Knox Suite - Enterprise Plan" to get a free trial of our services

5
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.933
then sign up for a Samsung account for Business.

6
00:00:31.433 --> 00:00:38.366
Once you've submitted your Samsung Knox application, inform your Samsung contact to approve your account. When you're approved 

7
00:00:38.366 --> 00:00:43.132
for Samsung Knox, you'll receive a confirmation email with your new Knox Customer ID.

8
00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:52.633
The Knox Suite - Enterprise Plan trial license you receive when you create a Samsung Knox account lets you try our services for 90 days 

9
00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:59.899
with up to 30 devices. To continue using Knox E-FOTA after that, you'll need to purchase a commercial license from a reseller.

10
00:01:00.666 --> 00:01:04.899
To do this, sign in to your Knox Admin Portal, and go to Licenses

11
00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:13.366
Here, click Actions, and Get a license, where you can find Knox license resellers to purchase a commercial Knox Suite - Enterprise Plan.

12
00:01:16.933 --> 00:01:24.966
When Knox E-FOTA runs on your devices, it prompts your device users to accept the terms and conditions, and the privacy policy. You can 

13
00:01:24.966 --> 00:01:33.032
configure Knox E-FOTA to skip this step so it can set up on your devices without device user interaction. To do this, click your account icon 

14
00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:40.366
on the Knox Admin Portal, then click Settings. Scroll down to Knox E-FOTA and click Privacy policy.

15
00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:45.732
Then, check "Skip Knox E-FOTA Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy", and click SAVE.

16
00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:58.766
Now you can connect Microsoft Intune with "Knox E-FOTA". To do this, sign in to your Microsoft Intune admin center, and go to 

17
00:01:58.766 --> 00:02:02.132
"Tenant administration", then "Connectors and tokens"

18
00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:10.299
Under "Connectors and tokens", go to "Firmware over-the-air update", and select Samsung on the list of OEMs.

19
00:02:11.333 --> 00:02:15.333
Click "Connect", and sign in to your Samsung Knox account.

20
00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:24.200
On the "Access requested" page, review the access permissions you're granting for Microsoft Intune, then click "Allow".

21
00:02:26.366 --> 00:02:30.766
The Samsung Firmware over-the-air connector status shows that you're connected.

22
00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:41.800
If you were previously using Knox E-FOTA on the Knox Admin Portal, note that connecting Microsoft Intune to Knox E-FOTA disables the 

23
00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:50.166
EMM groups feature in your Knox Admin Portal, and any devices that were previously added to Knox E-FOTA from an EMM group sync need to 

24
00:02:50.166 --> 00:02:52.999
be added again by registering them on Microsoft Intune.

25
00:02:54.900 --> 00:03:02.233
Also, Microsoft Intune only displays Android FOTA deployments that were created from its own console. When you assign a deployment to 

26
00:03:02.233 --> 00:03:06.733
your devices, it overwrites any existing campaigns previously assigned to those devices.

27
00:03:09.833 --> 00:03:14.299
Now you can create a device group for the Samsung devices you want to manage.

28
00:03:14.300 --> 00:03:18.800
In the Microsoft Intune admin center, go to "Groups" and create a new group. Give it a name and click "Create"

29
00:03:20.866 --> 00:03:23.099
Give it a name and click "Create".

30
00:03:26.266 --> 00:03:33.566
Next, deploy the required Samsung apps. You'll need both Knox E-FOTA and Knox Service Plugin installed on your devices.

31
00:03:33.566 --> 00:03:34.532
Go to "Apps"

32
00:03:36.266 --> 00:03:38.699
then "Android", and click "Create"

33
00:03:41.933 --> 00:03:45.933
Select "Store app" and "Managed Google Play app" as the app type.

34
00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:51.300
Search for "Knox E-FOTA" and add it

35
00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:58.466
then search for "Knox Service Plugin" and add that as well.

36
00:04:02.633 --> 00:04:05.233
Then assign both apps to your device group.

37
00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:08.033
Select the app

38
00:04:08.033 --> 00:04:09.966
and click Properties

39
00:04:12.066 --> 00:04:13.499
Edit the assignments

40
00:04:14.866 --> 00:04:16.232
and add your device group.

41
00:04:20.500 --> 00:04:23.033
Repeat those steps for Knox Service Plugin as well.

42
00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:34.866
Now configure Knox Service Plugin to automatically install and launch the Knox E-FOTA app.

43
00:04:36.233 --> 00:04:40.899
Go to "Devices" then "Configuration", and create a new policy.

44
00:04:43.766 --> 00:04:49.032
Select "Android Enterprise" as the platform, then "OEMConfig" as the profile type.

45
00:04:53.433 --> 00:04:55.099
Choose Knox Service Plugin

46
00:04:57.200 --> 00:05:02.066
and under "Device-wide policies", enable device policy controls.

47
00:05:03.833 --> 00:05:06.833
Then configure the "Firmware update policy"

48
00:05:07.666 --> 00:05:12.832
enable firmware controls and enable E-FOTA client installation and launch.

49
00:05:15.966 --> 00:05:19.966
Assign this profile to your device group and create the policy.

50
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:34.833
If you haven't already, enroll your Samsung devices on Microsoft Intune as company devices, and add them to your device group.

51
00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:38.766
Go to "Groups"

52
00:05:38.766 --> 00:05:42.366
select your device group

53
00:05:42.366 --> 00:05:46.232
click "Members", and add the devices you want to manage.

54
00:05:49.266 --> 00:05:58.199
Once your devices are ready, register them with Samsung Knox E-FOTA. Go to "Tenant administration" then "Connectors and tokens", 

55
00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.966
and select "Firmware over-the-air update".

56
00:06:02.933 --> 00:06:05.366
Choose Samsung from the OEM list

57
00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.600
and under "Register Devices with Samsung", click "Add groups".

58
00:06:12.633 --> 00:06:15.433
Select your device group and click "Register".

59
00:06:18.766 --> 00:06:22.266
You can check the status of device registration on the Monitor tab.

60
00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:31.233
Now you can create your firmware deployment. Go to "Devices"

61
00:06:32.833 --> 00:06:36.166
then "Android FOTA deployments", and click "Create".

62
00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:43.099
Select Samsung as the manufacturer

63
00:06:46.166 --> 00:06:50.166
give your deployment a name, and configure your deployment settings.

64
00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:59.000
Select the device models, sales codes, and CSCs you want to target. Then choose your "Update type".

65
00:07:00.433 --> 00:07:05.166
"Latest any" automatically pushes the newest available version to your devices

66
00:07:05.166 --> 00:07:09.899
while "Latest Up To Max OS Version" limits it to a specific OS version.

67
00:07:10.766 --> 00:07:15.999
"Lock current firmware version" maintains the current firmware on your devices

68
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:21.266
and "Select firmware version" lets you pick a specific version available to your targeted devices.

69
00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:31.633
You can set the date range when devices can perform firmware updates, and set installation and download time windows to control when 

70
00:07:31.633 --> 00:07:36.866
during the day devices can begin downloading and installing firmware, based on the device's local timezone.

71
00:07:37.333 --> 00:07:42.333
You can also set how many times device users are allowed to postpone a firmware update

72
00:07:42.333 --> 00:07:45.799
and how often they're reminded of a pending 
firmware update.

73
00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:52.166
You can also set device conditions needed for firmware installation.

74
00:07:52.166 --> 00:08:00.799
Require a minimum battery level before installation begins, require devices to be charging, or only perform firmware downloads 

75
00:08:00.800 --> 00:08:02.266
over certain network types.

76
00:08:05.166 --> 00:08:09.899
Once you've configured all your settings, assign the deployment to your device groups and click "Create".

77
00:08:12.733 --> 00:08:20.333
Your Samsung devices will now receive firmware updates according to the policy you've configured. You can monitor deployment status 

78
00:08:20.333 --> 00:08:25.466
and device compliance from the Android FOTA deployments page in the Microsoft Intune admin center.

79
00:08:26.233 --> 00:08:34.133
To learn more about using Knox E-FOTA on the Microsoft Intune admin center, see our documentation at docs.samsungknox.com.

80
00:08:34.133 --> 00:08:34.966
Thanks for watching!

